                <pb facs="0314" n="204" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg204"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60p2/29: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Latvia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Coleman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Riga</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-12T16:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 12,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Referring to paragraph 8 of Department’s telegram 19, May 16, 3 p.m. Latvian
                    Government has just informed Legation that paragraph 3 of protocol proposed by
                    it in its memorandum of March 5th, 1927,<anchor n="39" xml:id="d156-f1"/> refers
                    to article 19 of United States draft. Is Legation authorized to accept paragraph
                    3 in this context?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Coleman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
